== Overview and proof claims
PASS overview: coprime a,b>1 -> last gap ab-a-b; a 1-rod -> no positive gaps; gcd d>1 -> every non-multiple of d is a gap (all a != b <= 15); exceptions []
     (not claimed by the overview) gcd>1 pairs also miss a few small multiples of d: [(4, 6, [2]), (6, 9, [3]), (4, 10, [2, 6])]
PASS guide proof: for N > F the chosen j gives i >= 0, and F has no representation (coprime a,b <= 12)
PASS guide P8: 0, b, ..., (a-1)b have distinct remainders mod a when gcd(a,b)=1
PASS extension: 2/7 and 3/4 both have last gap 5

